{
  "message": "For everyday personal spending, these Rho-Bank options may fit:",
  "options": [
    {
      "card": "Bronze Rewards Card",
      "best_for": "No-annual-fee cash back",
      "details": "No annual fee; earns 1.0% cash back on eligible purchases. Rewards can be redeemed once your balance reaches $17."
    },
    {
      "card": "Silver Rewards Card",
      "best_for": "A straightforward everyday card",
      "details": "No annual fee, 0% introductory APR for the first year, then a standard 18.99% APR for carried balances. Earns 1.0% back outside bonus categories. A minimum credit score of 680 is listed."
    },
    {
      "card": "Platinum Rewards Card",
      "best_for": "Maximizing rewards on high everyday spending",
      "details": "Earns 10.0% cash back on eligible purchases, but carries a $200 annual fee. Rewards can be redeemed at $15 or more. The available information also notes a $150 annual-fee rebate for meeting a $7,500 monthly spending threshold."
    },
    {
      "card": "EcoCard",
      "best_for": "Sustainability-focused purchases",
      "details": "Earns sustainability points—5 points per dollar on green purchases and 1 point per dollar on other purchases. Points redeem at $0.01 each for statement or Rho-Bank checking-account credits."
    }
  ],
  "note": "Rho-Bank also references Gold Rewards, Diamond Elite, and Crypto-Cash Back personal cards, but I don’t have reliable current pricing and eligibility details for those options here. For a typical everyday card, Silver is the clearest no-fee choice; Platinum may be worthwhile only if your spending is high enough to offset its annual fee."
}
